From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 31 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: respond clockwise after the latest FFA chain link

Owner decision 2026-10-04, Domain Format Complete Rulebook v1.4 (Turn proceeding): restart FFA responses after the activating seat, ending with that seat. Existing pass records reset after each link and skip eliminated seats. Preserve the turn-player start of an open window, SEGOC and trigger ordering, the separate official Tag branch, and all two-player processor paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 field.cpp | 2 +-
 field.h   | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/field.cpp b/field.cpp
index 4822a0a..7b6f5c4 100644
--- a/field.cpp
+++ b/field.cpp
@@ -390,7 +390,7 @@ static uint8_t response_sequence(const field& f, uint8_t anchor, uint8_t* out, b
 			out[count++] = q;
 	};
 	if(f.n_teams == f.n_duelists) {
-		const uint8_t s = (anchor == tp) ? static_cast<uint8_t>(tp + 1) : tp;
+		const uint8_t s = anchor == DUELIST_NONE ? tp : static_cast<uint8_t>(anchor + 1);
 		for(uint8_t i = 0; i < f.n_duelists; ++i)
 			add(static_cast<uint8_t>(s + i));
 	} else if(anchor == DUELIST_NONE) {
diff --git a/field.h b/field.h
index 28d90ab..326e8c7 100644
--- a/field.h
+++ b/field.h
@@ -765,8 +765,8 @@ public:
 	// Response cursor for n_duelists > 2 (phase 2). All of these skip eliminated duelists and are
 	// not used when n_duelists == 2. out[] holds at most MAX_DUELISTS duelists; the result is the count.
 	// Order of the players who may answer after a Chain Link added by `anchor` (DUELIST_NONE = open window).
-	// Free for all: the turn player first, then clockwise (if the anchor is the turn player, the next
-	// duelist first and the turn player last). Tag: a+1, a+3, a+2, a; open window: tp, tp+1, tp+3, tp+2.
+	// Free for all: the next seat after the anchor first, then clockwise, with the anchor last.
+	// Open window: tp first, then clockwise. Tag: a+1, a+3, a+2, a; open window: tp, tp+1, tp+3, tp+2.
 	uint8_t response_order(uint8_t anchor, uint8_t* out) const;
 	// The first duelist in response_order(core.response_anchor) who has not passed (priorities[q] == 0).
 	uint8_t first_responder() const;
-- 
2.43.0

